WEBVTT

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.730
Say, Coconuts...

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:08.840
Hm?

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.740
There's something that I've been
wanting to tell you all this time.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:13.860
What is it?

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:15.490
You may not have noticed
since you're so dense,

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:21.540
so I'm just gonna be bold and spit it out.

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:26.330
Why...

00:00:26.330 --> 00:00:27.790
"Ice"

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:27.750
...is your shop...

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:29.380
...so...

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.420
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.460
...run down like this?

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.010
It's been...

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.450
...three months since then.

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:12.270
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.360
"Look after the shop. Thanks! Your father"

00:02:23.490 --> 00:02:26.750
Kokonotsu! I'm leaving the rest to you!

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.710
Damn you, dad!

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:38.660
I feel like eating some good food.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:44.560
Curry... Sushi... Ton-Tonkatsu...

00:02:46.220 --> 00:02:49.770
F-For some reason, I feel like I said
something that would summon Hotaru.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.060
Summoning... Right, like a summoning spell.

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.880
Yeah...

00:03:01.910 --> 00:03:05.080
H... Hotaru!

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:06.710
Thank you for wait--

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:15.710
You said it... Kokonotsu.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:18.050
You came running?! And you
were pushing yourself to act cool?!

00:03:22.470 --> 00:03:27.260
Ramune after a sprint really hits the spot.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:29.180
Why did you have to hurry like that?

00:03:29.180 --> 00:03:31.350
Tee-hee-hee... hee!

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:35.610
The time has finally come!

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:38.690
I thought of making it
"today's theme" so many times,

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.650
but then I would think,
"Maybe this isn't the right time."

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.610
So I've refrained from 
using it all this time.

00:03:42.610 --> 00:03:45.910
But today, you yourself have
summoned it, Kokonotsu!

00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.700
It's a legend in the 
deep-fried dagashi world!

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:50.830
It's the king of deep-fried foods
wearing a gold-colored coat!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:53.580
"Big Katsu"
"Special Sauce Flavor"

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:53.170
It's Big Katsu!

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:55.630
Big Katsu? Katsu...?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.090
"Magic Word"

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:59.090
So... "tonkatsu" is the magic
word to summon her, huh?

00:03:59.590 --> 00:04:03.470
Seriously... I've been anxiously waiting
for you to finally say that word.

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:05.090
"Anxious"

00:04:03.470 --> 00:04:05.340
Why did you have to wait for me to say it?

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:06.600
So...!

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:09.930
"Big Katsu"

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:12.890
Well... You know... I just figured
that this is kind of my thing, so...

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:17.150
"Ho"

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:17.150
Hm? Why are you acting embarrassed?
Did you bring that rice bowl yourself?

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.940
At any rate, Big Katsu, huh?

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:22.280
Tonkatsu was what I--

00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.410
Big Katsu... Tonkatsu...

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.410
Hotaru...

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:27.410
Hm?

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:31.600
Big Katsu isn't made of pork,
is it...? It's fish.

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:34.540
It's tonkatsu style!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.080
It's a style, Kokonotsu!

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:38.090
A-Ahh... Y-You're hurting me.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:40.090
"Ice"

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:40.090
That being said...

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.840
...in order to discuss it, I have to talk
about the secret origins of Big Katsu.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:46.590
Secret origins?!

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:49.810
The truth is, Kokonotsu,
Big Katsu started with...

00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:51.060
...squids!

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.140
Squids?!

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:57.060
The company that started it was developing a
product using squid as the main ingredient,

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:55.060
"Suguru" "President" "Employees"

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:57.060
"Processed Squids"

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.570
but they had a tough time because
they couldn't find any suppliers.

00:04:57.060 --> 00:05:00.570
"Suppliers" "President" "Employees"

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:05.200
Um...

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.320
But they didn't give up!

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:10.700
This time, they set their eyes on
fish instead and developed these!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:10.700
"Amatarakko Dried Squid Flavor" "Ika Ajiten"

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:16.330
"Amatarakko Dried Squid Flavor"

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:14.500
They made sheets from ground
fish and soaked them in a sauce.

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:16.330
That's Amatarakko, sweet dried squid style.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:19.710
"Ika Ajiten"

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.710
And this is Ika Ajiten,
the deep-fried one without any sauce!

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.550
Um, Hotaru...?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:24.880
They're both wonderful and I love them!

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.140
But... the developers
weren't satisfied, thinking,

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:32.470
"What can we do to surpass
the taste of real squids?!"

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.770
Hm?

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:34.600
What is it?

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.560
Well, they were trying to surpass dried
squid with dried squid style dagashi?

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:39.730
Yes, that's right.

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:42.230
"Employees"

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:43.900
Their hardship continued.
Even on a rainy day or a windy day.

00:05:43.900 --> 00:05:46.320
Even when it was painful and
tears welled up in their eyes...

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:48.240
...they never gave up...

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:50.740
"President" "Employees"

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.980
...in order to aim for even greater heights!

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:51.910
"Employees"

00:05:51.910 --> 00:05:54.750
"Employees"
"President"

00:05:56.330 --> 00:05:57.330
And...

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.180
And...?

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:05.550
"Ho"

00:06:01.630 --> 00:06:05.380
...they thought tonkatsu might be good,
so that's how Big Katsu was born.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:06.510
What?!

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:08.050
"Ho"
"Big Katsu"

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:08.050
Why?!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.550
Oh? You have an issue with that?

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:14.720
Well, it's not that.
The point of the story is kinda...

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:16.930
Besides, I wanted to eat tonkatsu.

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:20.810
Oh? Are you saying that Big
Katsu can't beat tonkatsu?!

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.480
You think only squids can surpass squids?

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:24.440
Wai--

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:27.070
Then what of all the blood,
sweat and tears they shed--

00:06:27.070 --> 00:06:29.070
Like I said, that's not the point!

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.160
That's not the point!

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.700
Forget winning or losing!

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:36.700
I think not being the real thing is exactly
what makes those dagashi appealing!

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:40.210
Big Katsu is delicious even
when you don't eat it with rice!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:41.580
And when you eat Ika Ajiten,

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.670
you wouldn't think, "I prefer real
squid tempura," would you?!

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:50.930
Well, I am glad that Big Katsu was born
as a result of their struggle, though.

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.470
I'd expect nothing less from you, Kokonotsu.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:56.520
Wha...

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:58.890
You dagashi genius, you!

00:06:58.890 --> 00:06:59.760
Huh?

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:03.560
A rising star! The successor 
of Shikada Dagashi!

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.520
Wha...?!

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:08.070
Good job putting your talents to use! Woohoo!

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:12.050
Your dad is a YouTuber!

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:13.570
Hotaru...

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:18.200
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.200
Please, just don't remind me...
about the YouTuber stuff.

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:20.830
And so, and so...

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:23.600
Pasta...

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.670
I kinda wanna eat pasta.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:30.670
Why don't you make it?
Actually, we have it in our menu, don't we?

00:07:30.670 --> 00:07:34.550
That's right. The pasta 
you make is pretty good.

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:37.100
Y-You think so?

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:42.190
It's true that people say that the
pasta I make is the best in town.

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:43.480
Our very small town.

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.690
Anyway, that's not what I meant!

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.320
I'm saying that I wanna eat it in a fancy
Italian restaurant with attractive garçons.

00:07:51.320 --> 00:07:54.700
We don't have a restaurant
like that in our town, do we?

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:55.620
No.

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.950
Do you want your big brother to make it?!

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:06.630
Thank you for waiting!

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:09.050
Looks like you're in a... bi... nd...

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.930
H-Hey, hey...

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:20.140
She came running again?! And she
was pushing herself to act cool again?!

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.640
"Endo"

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:26.810
Looks like you want to
eat pasta, huh, Master Saya?

00:08:26.810 --> 00:08:30.190
What? Ah! You know a good restaurant?!

00:08:31.110 --> 00:08:32.700
I'll make it!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:34.410
You're no better than my big brother.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:40.040
It's being... summoned... to this place!

00:08:37.570 --> 00:08:40.040
"Peperoncino"

00:08:40.540 --> 00:08:42.330
Um... What's this?

00:08:42.890 --> 00:08:44.290
You must be surprised...

00:08:44.960 --> 00:08:48.000
...to see that the world of
dagashi even includes spaghetti.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:53.010
No, it's not that. I wasn't impressed
by the novel idea or anything.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.510
At any rate, it really 
looks like cup noodles.

00:08:56.760 --> 00:09:00.270
This was originally created by
an instant noodle company.

00:09:01.270 --> 00:09:02.020
He's right.

00:09:02.430 --> 00:09:04.180
They used their know-how to
sublimate it into a dagashi product

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:08.770
that is as close to the real one
as possible! And this is that product!

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:10.190
"Sublimate"?

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:11.530
"Minute" "Second"

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:13.280
Once three minutes have 
passed, drain the water.

00:09:14.320 --> 00:09:17.870
Then, you stir in just a 
half of the soup powder.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:24.350
This is the king of Italian food in
the dagashi world... Peperoncino!

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.920
Now, Master Saya!

00:09:29.920 --> 00:09:31.300
O-Okay.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:37.050
It's good!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:38.010
Wow!

00:09:38.010 --> 00:09:39.470
Right?!

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:43.770
It's true that it's good... but I
feel like I know this taste.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:45.390
Ah...! That one...!

00:09:45.390 --> 00:09:47.560
"Salt-flavored yakisoba"

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:47.560
Instant salt-flavored yakisoba!

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:50.310
I-It's not pasta!

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:54.530
You noticed, huh? That's our Master Saya.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:58.070
Take a close look at this packet.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:10:00.240
"Soup Powder"
"Ramen style: Entire packet"
"Pasta style: Half packet"

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:00.240
Ah! Pasta style...!

00:10:00.620 --> 00:10:04.950
That's right. It says "style."
On top of that, there's ramen style, too!

00:10:05.450 --> 00:10:10.460
If you put in all of the soup powder without
draining the water, it becomes ramen style!

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:14.170
Anything goes, huh?
This "style" thing is amazing!

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:18.300
Ah, but do you just ditch the
remaining half of the powder?

00:10:19.130 --> 00:10:22.050
Non, non. It gets even better.

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:27.810
Once you finish eating, put the
remaining powder in the container...

00:10:28.390 --> 00:10:30.240
...and pour hot water into it.

00:10:31.310 --> 00:10:34.190
Now it becomes an after-meal soup.

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:36.940
T-This pasta style stuff is amazing!

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.700
I thoroughly enjoyed it.

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.950
It was delicious!

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.370
It's like, "Ottimo," right?!

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:48.790
"O-Ottimo"?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:52.210
That's the superlative form of
the Italian word for "delicious."

00:10:52.670 --> 00:10:54.840
Now, everyone together!

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.340
What?!

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.340
Ottimo!

00:10:57.550 --> 00:11:00.130
O-Ottimo...

00:11:00.130 --> 00:11:01.930
I can't hear you!

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.850
Ottimo!

00:11:05.140 --> 00:11:06.390
One more time!

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:10.140
"Big Katsu, Peperoncino, and..."

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:09.940
Ottimo!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time: Baseball Board Game Gum,
Pop Pop Boat, and..."

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:11.410
Next time: "Baseball Board Game Gum,
Pop Pop Boat, and..."

00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:14.180
Now, I'll play with Master Saya in the bath!
